>> title: Yellow Rice
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: rice, turmeric, middle eastern, stock, side
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: yellow rice, turmeric rice, seasoned rice, halal cart rice, cart rice, basmati rice, arroz amarillo, riz asfar
>> pairs-with: chicken-shawarma, white-sauce, rice-pilaf
>> servings: 6
>> time: 45 min
>> step.1: rinse until the water runs clear
>> step.2: bloom the turmeric and cumin in butter
>> step.3: toast the rice 2 min
>> step.4: simmer 15 min, lid on
>> step.5: steam off the heat 10 min, then fork

Rinse @basmati rice{2%cups}(400 g) in a bowl of cold water, pouring off and refilling four or five times until the water stops going white, then drain it well. What you are rinsing away is loose surface starch, and it is the difference between separate grains under the meat and a scoop that arrives as one lump.

Bloom @ground turmeric{1 1/2%tsp}, @cumin seed{1%tsp} and @yellow onion{1%small}(diced fine) in @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(45 g) in a #saucepan{} over medium heat ~fry{3%min}, until the butter is orange and the onion is soft. Turmeric and not saffron — the yellow on this counter is turmeric, it is cheap, and any recipe reaching for saffron here is describing a different plate.

Toast @&(~2)rinsed rice{} in @&(~1)spiced butter{} ~toast{2%min}, stirring, until every grain is coated and slightly translucent at the edge.

Simmer @chicken stock{3%cups}(700 mL) and @kosher salt{1 1/2%tsp} with @&(~1)toasted rice{}, covered, over the lowest heat ~simmer{15%min}. Stock and not water: this rice is seasoned all the way through, which is why it holds its own under a sauce.

Take @&(~1)rice{} off the heat and let it ~steam{10%min} with the lid still on and undisturbed, then fork it through. Lifting the lid early drops the steam that finishes the top layer, and no amount of extra cooking gets it back.
